.Dd August 6, 2026
.Dt FIT-WINDOWS 1
.Os "Mac OS X"
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm fit-windows
.Nd resize an app's windows to fill the screen
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm Ar app-name
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
resizes a running application's windows to fill the available display space.
It is equivalent to pressing the green menu-bar button of every app window \
with the Option key held.
.Bl -tag -width 4n
.It Fl h , -help
Print a short usage message,
then terminate.
.It Fl v , -version
Print the program's version string,
then terminate.
.It Ar app-name
An application whose windows are to be resized.
Its human-readable name
.Pq Dv kMDItemDisplayName
must be provided,
with or without a trailing
.Dq .app .
Attempting to specify an application by its bundle ID will
.Em not
work!
.El
.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width 4n
.It Pa ~/.files/etc/darwin/fit-windows.scpt
Path to
.Nm Ap s
AppleScript executable.
.It Pf $ Dv TMPDIR Ns Pa /TemporaryItems/tmp.SPDisplaysReporter.plist
Temporary
.Xr plist 5
file created when parsing the XML output of
.Xr system_profiler 8 .
.El
.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Resize every document window in Preview.app:
.Dl Nm Li Preview
.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -ohang
.It Sy "execution error: No application name specified (-1715)"
The
.Ar app-name
parameter was omitted or set to the empty string.
.It Sy "execution error: Parameter error. (-50)"
An unrecognised option was passed to
.Nm .
.It Sy "execution error: Application isn\(cqt running. (-600)"
The specified application isn't currently running.
.El
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lsappinfo 1 ,
.Xr osascript 1
.
.Sh HISTORY
A simpler version of this script named
.Ql fit-terminal.scpt
was written on January 31, 2019,
and was limited to resizing the windows of Terminal.app.
Its usage was eventually obviated by the addition of shell aliases \
that resized the terminal's window(s) using ANSI escape codes.
The script was later deleted on April 8, 2024.
.Pp
In August 2026,
a similar script was penned that targets any running application.
.
